4. Grid View Design
   The grid (time axis) view was designed with reference to a proposed
   implementation by GitHub user @lenaxia, offered as pull request #339.
   https://github.com/alexpfau/calendar-card-pro/pull/339

   No code was carried across. That branch was written against a much earlier
   revision of this card and had fallen some eight hundred commits behind, so
   it could not be merged and was instead read for its design decisions. Two
   in particular are theirs: positioning events by wall-clock minutes rather
   than by elapsed milliseconds, which is what keeps placement correct on
   daylight-saving transition days, and drawing a multi-day all-day event as
   one continuous banner with continuation marks rather than as a separate
   chip in each day it covers.
